{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6f2f5c1e-2b7a-4a4e-9d3e-portfolio0001",
    "name": "Restful Booker API Tests",
    "description": "Automated API tests for https://restful-booker.herokuapp.com/ — token auth, booking CRUD lifecycle with dynamic data, and negative scenarios.\n\nIndependent QA portfolio project by Elene Molashvili (https://github.com/lenossm).\n\nRun order matters inside 'Booking lifecycle (chained)': the folder creates a booking, verifies it, updates it, deletes it and verifies the deletion, passing the booking ID and expected values between requests through collection variables.\n\nKnown Restful Booker quirks asserted as actual behaviour and documented in docs/defect-samples.md: /auth answers 200 with a 'reason' body instead of 401 (DEF-API-001), successful DELETE answers 201 (DEF-API-002), writes to nonexistent bookings answer 405 instead of 404 (DEF-API-003).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ping — service is up",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201 (documented health-check response)', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response time is within the documented 5000 ms budget', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(5000);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ping", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["ping"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth — positive",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create token with valid credentials",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Content-Type is application/json', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains a non-empty string token', function () {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('token');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a('string').and.to.have.length.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Chain: store the token for authenticated write requests.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
